**Goal** — Add the four write-path ChatThread columns, accept the runner's `threadWrite` capability, make placement treat PUBLISH/DISCARD thread jobs as model-free write jobs, and send the thread title in the ASSIGN.

**Motivation** — C1 gave the runner write_doc, Publish, stale start and Discard, but the deployed API never queues them: its capability parser drops `threadWrite` and nothing records write-path state.

**Approach** — verbatim from the spec:

Migration `apps/api/prisma/migrations/20261015090000_thread_handoff/migration.sql`:
```sql
ALTER TABLE "ChatThread" ADD COLUMN "writtenPaths" TEXT[] NOT NULL DEFAULT ARRAY[]::TEXT[];
ALTER TABLE "ChatThread" ADD COLUMN "publishedSha" TEXT;
ALTER TABLE "ChatThread" ADD COLUMN "specPublished" BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false;
ALTER TABLE "ChatThread" ADD COLUMN "lastWrite" JSONB;
```

Capability and placement:
- `parseCapabilitiesCore`: `threadWrite` absent -> absent from the result; `true` -> `threadWrite: true`; any other value -> `CapabilityValidationError` with reason `threadWrite` (strict, like `configJobs`).
- `PlacementService` passes `action: threadAssign.action` into `PlacementJob.thread` at both call sites.
- `firstMisfit` thread branch, in order: `threads_disabled`, `protocol`, then for `action` `PUBLISH` / `DISCARD`: `!runner.capabilities.threadWrite` -> `thread_write` (no backend check); for any other `action`, including an absent one: the existing backend check; then `thread_capacity` for every action. The existing placement test fixtures build `thread` without `action` and keep their results.
- C2-D3: a `PUBLISH` or `DISCARD` job needs no model, so placement skips the backend check for it and instead requires `threadWrite`. `thread_write` is not a permanent misfit (a runner restart or re-probe clears it).

Symbol changes: `ChatThread` (schema.prisma:1057) adds `writtenPaths String[] @default([])`, `publishedSha String?`, `specPublished Boolean @default(false)`, `lastWrite Json?`. `ChatThreadRecord` / `ThreadDto` add `writtenPaths: string[]`, `publishedSha: string | null`, `specPublished: boolean`, `lastWrite: ThreadWriteResult | null` (mapThread in prisma-chat-thread.repository.ts maps them). `PlacementJob.thread` (placement-rules.ts:32) and `toPlacementJob`'s third parameter (placement-rules.ts:160) go from `{ backend; enabled }` to `{ backend; enabled; action?: ThreadAction }`; absent behaves as `SESSION`. `MisfitReason` / `firstMisfit` (placement-rules.ts:10,101) add `'thread_write'`; the reason enum lists in `jobs/dto/fleet-job.dto.ts:107` and `dashboard/dashboard.types.ts:109` (`MISFIT_REASONS`) gain `thread_write`. `findThreadAssign` (prisma-fleet-job.repository.ts:192) returns `title` from `ChatThread.title`. The `record` fixture in `threads.service.spec.ts` (typed `ChatThreadRecord`) gains `writtenPaths: []`, `publishedSha: null`, `specPublished: false`, `lastWrite: null`; every assertion stays. Run `bunx prisma validate`, `bun run db:generate` in apps/api and `bun run generate` at repo root (`thread_write` reaches apps/cli/src/generated/types.gen.ts).

**Scope** — In: migration, schema, ChatThreadRecord/ThreadDto fields, ThreadWriteResult type, capability parsing, placement misfit, MISFIT_REASONS enums, findThreadAssign title. Out: folding write-path lines (US-002), Publish/Discard routes and createThreadJob (US-003/US-004), the `handoff` field on the thread detail (US-006).

**Interface**
```ts
// chat-thread.domain.ts; also the `lastWrite` JSON shape
export type ThreadWriteResult =
  | { kind: 'published'; jobId: string; at: string; sha: string; paths: string[]; ignored: string[] }
  | { kind: 'publish_failed'; jobId: string; at: string; reason: string }
  | { kind: 'discarded'; jobId: string; at: string; sha: string }
  | { kind: 'discard_failed'; jobId: string; at: string; reason: string };
// PlacementJob.thread: { backend; enabled; action?: ThreadAction }
// MisfitReason adds 'thread_write'
```

**Goal** — Enforce one active job per thread on Send, extract `createThreadJob`, and add `POST /projects/:slug/threads/:id/publish`.

**Motivation** — A thread ends with a spec draft in a chat reply that the user must copy by hand because the deployed API never queues `THREAD_PUBLISH` or a `PUBLISH` job.

**Approach** — verbatim from the spec:

C2-D2: the one-active-job rule (umbrella §5.1) counts every non-terminal `FleetJob` with the thread's `threadId` (`THREAD` of any action, `PLAN`, `RUN`).

C2-D3 (budget): placement still cancels a queued job whose budget scope is paused (`placement.service.ts:70`), so the Publish route refuses a paused scope up front with the same `BudgetPausedException` (409 `fleet.budgetPaused`) that Send throws, instead of creating a job that placement would cancel.

C2-D5: Publish on a live session sends `THREAD_PUBLISH` and is allowed with an empty `writtenPaths` (the runner computes the real dirty set and answers `published` with `paths: []` when nothing changed). Publish without a live session creates a `PUBLISH` job only when `writtenPaths` is non-empty.

`activeThreadJob(threadId)` (repository, private to the module): the latest (`queuedAt desc, id desc`) `FleetJob` with that `threadId` and a state in `ACTIVE_STATES`, any command, with its `FleetThreadTurn.action` (null for `PLAN` / `RUN`).

`sendMessage` additionally refuses 409 `threads.busy` after `sendRefusal` passes, when `activeThreadJob` is a `PLAN` or `RUN`, or a `THREAD` job whose action is `PUBLISH` or `DISCARD`.

`POST /projects/:slug/threads/:id/publish` (creator, users only, 200, body `{}`, returns `{ jobId: string | null }`). Inside `txManager.run`, after the same job-then-thread locks as `sendMessage`, the checks run in this order:

1. thread missing -> 404 `threads.notFound`; caller not the creator -> 403 `threads.notCreator`;
2. `threadsEnabled` false -> 409 `threads.disabled`; `status = ARCHIVED` -> 409 `threads.archived`;
3. `thread.runnerId` null -> 409 `threads.nothingToPublish`;
4. runner offline -> 409 `threads.runnerOffline`; runner `protocolVersion < 4` or no `capabilities.threadWrite` -> 409 `threads.runnerOutdated`; a paused budget scope of the thread (`jobGateKeys` with the pinned runner, as Send) -> `BudgetPausedException`;
5. active job is a `THREAD` `SESSION` job: `UPLOADING` or a `THREAD_CLOSE` queued at its epoch -> 409 `threads.closing`; `QUEUED` / `ASSIGNED`, or a message of the thread `pending` / `streaming` -> 409 `threads.turnRunning`; otherwise (`RUNNING`, idle) queue `THREAD_PUBLISH` with payload `{}` at the job's `leaseEpoch`, notify the runner after commit, return `{ jobId: null }`;
6. any other active job -> 409 `threads.busy`;
7. no active job: `writtenPaths` empty -> 409 `threads.nothingToPublish`; otherwise `createThreadJob(thread, 'PUBLISH')`, place it after commit, return `{ jobId }`.

`createThreadJob(thread, action, message?)` (private, extracted from `sendMessage`) creates the `THREAD` job with the values `sendMessage` uses today (`feature: thread-<id>`, `ref: baseRef`, `pinnedRunnerId: thread.runnerId`, `bashMode: raw`); `maxCostUsd` is the remaining cap for `SESSION` (today's value) and the fixed string `'0'` for `PUBLISH` / `DISCARD`, which spend nothing and must pass the runner's `COST_RE` (`apps/runner/src/executor/nax-process.ts:7`) even when the thread is over its cap. Publish and Discard therefore ignore the thread cost cap (no `threads.costCap`). Its `FleetThreadTurn` gets `action`, `initialMessageId: message?.id ?? null`, `resume: action === 'SESSION' && <a previous THREAD job of the thread whose turn action is SESSION exists>`, `instructions` from `buildThreadInstructions`, `backend`, `skills`), the `QUEUED` state event and the `job.dispatched` activity, and maps `DuplicateActiveJobError` to 409 `threads.busy` for `PUBLISH` / `DISCARD` and `threads.turnRunning` for `SESSION` (today's mapping).

i18n: add to both `apps/api/src/i18n/en/threads.json` and `apps/api/src/i18n/zh/threads.json`: `busy` "Another job of this thread is still active" and `nothingToPublish` "Thread has nothing to publish" (shape `{ "<key>": { "409": "<text>" } }`).

C2-D4: the terminal hook (`ThreadJobEffects.onJobEnded`) is unchanged: `closeSnapshot` only touches a session whose `jobId` is the ending job, and a `PUBLISH` / `DISCARD` job never starts a session.

Symbol changes: `PrismaChatThreadRepository.sendMessage` (prisma-chat-thread.repository.ts:153) creates the THREAD job inline today; job creation moves to private `createThreadJob`. `ChatThreadRepository` (threads/domain/chat-thread.domain.ts) adds `publish(projectId, threadId, userId)`. Add the controller route, service delegation, add the publish route's happy path (a `PUBLISH` job queued) and one refusal (`threads.nothingToPublish`) to the threads block of `apps/api/test/e2e/api-endpoint/endpoint.e2e.spec.ts` (existing tests unchanged), and run `bun run generate` at the repo root.

**Scope** — In: activeThreadJob, sendMessage busy refusal, createThreadJob extraction (SESSION and PUBLISH; DISCARD action is accepted by the signature), publish repository/service/controller route, i18n busy and nothingToPublish. Out: Discard route, publish ack handling, instructions text and stop/end-session noSession (US-004); Plan/Run (US-006/US-007).

**Interface**
```ts
// ChatThreadRepository adds
publish(projectId: string, threadId: string, userId: string): Promise<{ jobId: string | null }>;
// private
createThreadJob(thread, action: ThreadAction, message?): Promise<FleetJob>
```

**Goal** — Add `POST /projects/:slug/threads/:id/plan` backed by a thread-aware `FleetJobsService.dispatch`, set `expectBranch` on a thread PLAN's ASSIGN, and expose `handoff` on the thread detail.

**Motivation** — After Publish, the user must be able to dispatch PLAN on `feat/<feature>` pinned to the thread's runner, with at most one active job per thread.

**Approach** — verbatim from the spec:

C2-D6: a thread's `PLAN` and `RUN` use `ref = feat/<feature>`, `feature = <thread feature>`, `pinnedRunnerId = thread.runnerId` and `threadId`; `PLAN` adds `planFrom = specPath`. The ASSIGN of a `PLAN` with a `threadId` carries `expectBranch` equal to the job's `ref`.

C2-D2: for `PLAN` / `RUN` the one-active-job check runs inside `FleetJobsService.dispatch`'s transaction, right before `createJob`, under a `ChatThread` row lock, so two concurrent requests cannot both pass.

`POST /projects/:slug/threads/:id/plan` (creator, users only, 201, body `PlanThreadDto { profiles?: string[]; maxCostUsd?: number }`, returns `DispatchResultDto`). The controller first checks the caller's project ability `CREATE FleetJob` (as thread create does, `threads.controller.ts`), else 403 `projects`. `maxCostUsd` is a number validated like `DispatchFleetJobDto.maxCostUsd`; when omitted it is `THREAD_HANDOFF_DEFAULT_MAX_COST_USD = 5` (the dispatch form's default, `apps/web/lib/fleet-dispatch.ts:69`), a constant exported from `threads/thread-handoff.ts`. `ThreadsService.plan` checks in order: 404 / 403; `threads.disabled`; `threads.archived`; `specPublished` false -> 409 `threads.notPublished`; then calls `FleetJobsService.dispatch(userId, projectId, { repoId, command: 'PLAN', ref: 'feat/<feature>', feature, planFrom: specPath, profiles, maxCostUsd, pinnedRunnerId: thread.runnerId }, { threadId })`. The DTO validation mirrors `DispatchFleetJobDto` (jobs/dto/dispatch-fleet-job.dto.ts) for `profiles` (at most 8 strings of at most 64 characters) and `maxCostUsd`. DTOs go in `threads/dto/thread-handoff.dto.ts`.

`FleetJobsService.dispatch` (jobs/fleet-jobs.service.ts:63) with `opts.threadId` (opts become `{ scheduleId?, ticketActor?, threadId?: string }`): `dispatch` spreads `threadId: opts.threadId` into the `createJob` input (`NewFleetJob.threadId`, `fleet-job.domain.ts:115`; `normalizeDispatch` does not carry it); inside the existing transaction, before `createJob`, the new `IFleetJobRepository.lockIdleThread(threadId): Promise<boolean>` (true when idle; `jobs/domain/fleet-job.domain.ts:198`) runs `SELECT ... FROM "ChatThread" WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE` and counts `FleetJob` rows with that `threadId` in `ACTIVE_STATES` (jobs/job-state.ts:8); a count above 0 -> 409 `threads.busy` (ConflictAppException). A `DuplicateActiveJobError` (the `(repoId, feature)` index: a dispatch-form job of the same feature is active) keeps today's 409 `fleet.jobs` with `activeJobId`.

`buildAssignPayload` (jobs/assign-payload.ts): a `PLAN` job with a non-null `threadId` gets `expectBranch: job.ref`; every other job has no `expectBranch` key.

`ChatThreadDetail.handoff: { plan: ThreadHandoffJob | null; run: ThreadHandoffJob | null }`, where `ThreadHandoffJob = { jobId: string; state: string; stateReason: string | null }` is the thread's latest (`queuedAt desc, id desc`) job of that command. `ChatThreadRepository` adds `handoff(threadId)`; `GET /projects/:slug/threads/:id` returns it (`ThreadDetailDto` gains `handoff`).

i18n: add `notPublished` "Publish the thread's spec before planning" to both `apps/api/src/i18n/en/threads.json` and `apps/api/src/i18n/zh/threads.json`.

Tests/gates: in `apps/api/src/fleet/fleet-openapi.contract.spec.ts` the `ThreadDetailDto` assertion uses `toContain`, so it stays; add `handoff` to it (runner summary key list at line 41 is unchanged because `threadWrite` is not exposed). Add the plan route's happy path (201, job `PLAN` with `threadId`) and `threads.notPublished` to the threads block of `apps/api/test/e2e/api-endpoint/endpoint.e2e.spec.ts` (existing tests unchanged). Run `bun run generate` at the repo root.

**Scope** — In: plan route/service/DTO, dispatch threadId option and lockIdleThread, buildAssignPayload expectBranch, handoff on thread detail, notPublished i18n. Out: the Run route and `notPlanned` (US-007), runner-side expectBranch (US-005), write-path folding that sets specPublished (US-002), web UI (C3).

**Interface**
```ts
// threads/thread-handoff.ts
export const THREAD_HANDOFF_DEFAULT_MAX_COST_USD = 5;
export interface ThreadHandoffJob { jobId: string; state: string; stateReason: string | null }
// ChatThreadDetail
handoff: { plan: ThreadHandoffJob | null; run: ThreadHandoffJob | null }
// threads/dto/thread-handoff.dto.ts
class PlanThreadDto { profiles?: string[]; maxCostUsd?: number }
// IFleetJobRepository adds
lockIdleThread(threadId: string): Promise<boolean>;
// FleetJobsService.dispatch opts: { scheduleId?; ticketActor?; threadId?: string }
```
